  "body": "## What changed\n\n- New post `assets/posts/richauto.cps` for the RichAuto DSP A11 router controller.\n- The post is registered as `\"RichAuto DSP A11\"` in `BUILTINS` (`crates/app/src/posting_files.rs`). It comes after Mach4, at the end of the mill posts.\n- The output follows the `.mmg` program that a Laguna Swift A11 runs (#1907, comment of 2026-11-18). The comment of 2026-11-18 on this issue names that program as the conformance target.\n  - The file extension is `.mmg`.\n  - Each block has a sequence number: `N10`, then steps of 10. Comment lines and the `%` line have no number.\n  - There are no spaces between words.\n  - Lengths have three decimals. `F` is mm/min with one decimal.\n  - Rapid is `G00` and feed is `G1`. The spindle starts with `M03S<rpm>` and stops with `M05`.\n  - An axis word or an `F` word that does not change is not written.\n  - The program ends with `M30` and then a `%` line.\n- The setup block is `G21G90G17`. The post writes no `G54`, `G40`, `G80`, `G91.1`, `G94`, `G43`, `G49`, `T` or `M6` word.\n- Offset 1 is the work origin that the operator sets on the pendant. Offsets 2 and higher are refused by name.\n- Arcs use incremental `I`/`J`/`K` (`AbsCntr = Off`). An arc of more than 180 degrees is split.\n- Drilling cycles are expanded to plain `G00`/`G1` moves, with the floor dwell and the bore spindle stop and restart.\n- The `SpindleDwellMs` option writes `G04P<ms>` after the spindle start. The default is 0.\n- The post refuses these by name: tapping, `G41`/`G42`, probing, rotary moves, `G96`, a second tool, an inch document, a bad rpm, a bad coolant, and a missing or low clearance plane.\n- The post writes header notes (#2996) and WARN records as `(...)` comments.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe shipped posts do not run safely on an A11. They write `G91.1`, `G53`, `T.. M6`, `G43` and canned cycles. A basic A11 firmware can refuse these words.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `crates/post/tests/script_richauto.rs` and `crates/post/tests/richauto_safety/mod.rs`: 41 tests, including the 11 recorded-stream goldens of `post_suite!`.\n- The pin `richauto_writes_the_a11_mmg_block_format` was red on the older held script (format without `N`, `%`): `the program ends with %`. It is green on the new script.\n- On `upstream/main` all the pins are red, because the post does not exist.\n- `crates/app/tests/conformance.rs`: RichAuto is added to `POSTS`, `REFUSED` (`tap_plate`, \"tapping\"), the synth stream (G54, no tap) and `EXTENSIONS` (`mmg`). All 7 tests pass.\n- `crates/post/tests/comment_escape.rs`: the count of shipped posts goes from 20 to 21.\n- Mutations. Each mutant was run against the pins, then the script was restored and the pins were green again:\n  - no final `%` line: 8 tests red, including `richauto_writes_the_a11_mmg_block_format`;\n  - spaces between words: 18 tests red;\n  - no modal word omission: 11 tests red, including `unchanged_axis_and_feed_words_are_left_out`;\n  - no `onComment` hook: `comment_escape::header_notes_use_each_shipped_dialect_and_keep_the_full_surface_bound` red;\n  - no sequence step (all blocks `N0`): 7 tests red.\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`, base `dfbe0d8a5`): 752 of 753 steps pass. The one red step is `slot_dxf_sketch::a_slot_outline_seeds_the_slot_and_cuts_it_to_size`. It fails in the same way on unchanged `upstream/main` (stale golden `slot_dxf_outline.cl`). I filed it as #3293.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` and `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Heavy lanes: not run.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\n- No existing golden changed.\n- New: 12 conformance goldens in `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/richauto/`, `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/synth_richauto.nc`, and 11 recorded goldens in `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/richauto/` (6 programs, 5 refusals). I read each one. The arc centres are correct with a non-zero origin.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No program ran on an A11 or on the friend's Laguna Swift.\n- The A11 response to `G21G90G17`, to `G2`/`G3` with incremental centres and to `G04P` is not confirmed. The sample program has no setup block, no arcs and no dwell.\n- The sample program has CRLF line ends. This post writes LF.\n- `axisInversion` is not declared. The engine refuses a machine with an inverted axis by name. Grbl 1.1 is the same.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nThese open PRs add rows to the same lists (`BUILTINS`, or the lists in `conformance.rs`). They touch other posts and do not change the same function: #3160, #3058, #2999, #2993, #2992, #2981, #2979, #2978, #2974, #2972, #2969, #2968, #2964, #2955, #2951, #2646, #2515. The PR that merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: New built-in post \"RichAuto DSP A11\" for RichAuto A11 routers (Laguna Swift, Grizzly): .mmg files with N numbers, one tool, drilling as plain moves, named refusals for tapping, cutter compensation and probing.\n\nFixes #1914\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
